% ======================================================================================== 6 Risk
\section{Risk management}\label{sec:risk}
\para{Limits and de-risking} Each order is at most << V('risk.order_usd') >> and each match at most
<< V('risk.netcap') >> shares net at 5--95¢, which caps the open position at << V('risk.maxloss') >>, not the loss:
buying both sides of a match can lock in more (worst match << V('risk.pm.worst.is') >> IS,
<< V('risk.pm.worst.oos') >> OOS), so a << V('risk.daily_stop') >> daily loss ends the day. Set in advance, we stop if
the score feed is over << V('risk.feed_stale') >>\,s stale, vision over << V('risk.vision_stale') >>\,s stale, or
latency above its 95th percentile; we halve size if the trailing 30-day edge falls below << V('pol.trail_half') >>¢,
and stop if it reaches zero, if drawdown hits << V('pol.dd_stop') >>, or if the venue changes its fee or hold. None
fired in sample (trailing edge \(\geq\)<< V('risk.trail_min') >>¢, worst day << V('v2.is.worstday_usd') >>).

\para{Model, concentration and tail risk} Wrong CV calls always fill, so an out call trades only at confidence
\(\geq\)0.95 and one confirmed false call halts the day; << V('cv.phantom.pre') >> phantom calls a day would erase the
pre-registered 1\,s OOS P\&L (<< V('cv.phantom.cal') >> post hoc). The top five copied wallets carry
<< V('conc.top5.is') >> of v2's P\&L in sample and << V('conc.top5.oos') >> out of sample; without them v2 earns
<< V('conc.ex5.oos.c') >>¢ << V('conc.ex5.oos.ci') >> OOS. A per-wallet cap (<< V('wcap.W') >> a day, and a wallet
whose trailing edge turns negative is retired), chosen in sample from << V('wcap.n') >> more variants and pre-registered at \texttt{<< V('wcap.commit') >>},
ran once on the burned OOS (non-blind): << V('wcap.oos.c') >>¢ << V('wcap.oos.ci') >>, Sharpe << V('wcap.oos.sr') >>,
worst day << V('wcap.oos.worstday') >> instead of << V('wcap.base.oos.worstday') >>; it costs << V('wcap.is.cost') >> of
in-sample dollars and the top five still carry << V('wcap.oos.top5') >>. The UMA oracle settles markets \citep{pmuma},
US persons may only close positions \citep{pmgeoblock}, and courtsiding breaches ticket terms \citep{itf2026}. Factor
risk is nil (largest factor \(|t| = << V('fac.max_t') >>\); \(\alpha\) has \(t = << V('fac.alpha_t') >>\))
\citep{fama1993,carhart1997}.

